BEGIN:VEVENT
IMAGE;VALUE=URI;DISPLAY=BADGE;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://diverseworks.org/wp
 -content/uploads/2026/04/NuestroWorld-Calendar-size-169.png
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://diverseworks.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/0
 4/NuestroWorld-Calendar-size-169.png
UID:tHqA8NKVjgx0PGFG7wFMr
SUMMARY:Jesus Benavente: NUESTROWORLD
DTSTAMP:20260811T095926Z
DTSTART:20260813T000000Z
DESCRIPTION:Opening Thursday\, August 13\, 2026 | 6 – 8 pmDiverseWorks @ 56
	01 B Navigation Blvd\nNUESTROWORLD is a satirical solo installation by Bro
	oklyn-based artist Jesus Benavente. Featuring newly commissioned works\, N
	uestroWorld opens on Thursday\, August 13\, 2026\, transforming 5601 B Nav
	igation Blvd\, Houston\, TX 77011 into a fictional visitor center for Nues
	troWorld\, encouraging guests to explore Houston beyond the gallery walls 
	and experience the city as an amusement park. The installation will be on 
	view through September 13\, 2026\, with a closing party on September 11. G
	allery hours are Thursday – Saturday\, 12 – 6 pm. Admission is free. \nThr
	ough satire and spectacle\, NuestroWorld examines how cities construct ide
	ntity through tourism\, branding\, memory\, and myth\, inviting audiences 
	to reconsider Houston’s past and present. The exhibition draws inspiration
	 from pivotal moments in Houston and Texas history\, including the opening
	 of the Astrodome and Astroworld in the late 1960s\, Selena’s iconic Houst
	on Livestock Show & Rodeo performances in the 1990s\, and the folklore sur
	rounding Santa Anna’s capture following the Battle of San Jacinto in 1836\
	, highlighting the city’s recurring cycles of ambition\, folly\, and heart
	break. The title plays on “Astroworld” and uses Spanglish to create the ph
	rase “The World Is Ours\,” reframing Houston’s cultural mythology through 
	humor\, nostalgia\, and critical reflection. \nOpening ReceptionThursday\,
	 August 13\, 6 – 8 pmArtist and Curator Talk: 6:45 pm \nClosing PartyFrida
	y\, September 11\, 2026\, 6 – 8 pm \n6 pm: NuestroWorld x Nuestra Palabra:
	 The Words are OursFeaturing writers unearthing our gente’s role in buildi
	ng thebricks\, mortar\, and heart of Htown. Master of Ceremonies:Tony Diaz
	\, El Librotraficante\, backed up by an army of poetas. \n7 pm: special pe
	rformance by CTS Trio – Queen of Tejano & Latin Tribute BandPerforming the
	 greatest Latin hits of all time. \nARTIST BIO:\nJesus Benavente is a visu
	al artist based in Brooklyn\, New York\, and born in San Antonio\, Texas. 
	Benavente earned an MFA from Rutgers University and attended Skowhegan Sch
	ool of Painting and Sculpture. Recent exhibitions and performances include
	 Reception Rome\, Italy\; the Whitney Museum of American Art\, New York\; 
	Queens Museum\; LTD Los Angeles\; Performa 13\, New York\; Acre Projects\,
	 Chicago\; Chinati Foundation\, Marfa\; the Neuberger Museum of Art\, Purc
	hase\, NY\; Shin Museum of Art\, South Korea\; Vox Populi\, Philadelphia\;
	 and Socrates Sculpture Park\, New York. \nWebsite: http://jesusbenavente.
	netInstagram: @testotesto3 \n \n\nhttps://diverseworks.org/event/jesus-ben
	avente-nuestroworld/\n\nFrom DiverseWorks
URL:https://diverseworks.org/event/jesus-benavente-nuestroworld/
LOCATION:DiverseWorks\, @ 5601 B Navigation Blvd & Various Locations\, 5601
	 B Navigation Blvd\, Houston\, TX\, 77011\, United States
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:diverseworks
CATEGORIES:DiverseWorks
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT768H
END:VEVENT
